{
  "title": "Scaling multiplies per-item (\"each\") alternative measurements",
  "description": "The parser stores per-item sizes as alternatives with an \" each\" unit: \"2 packages marshmallows (10 ounces each)\" → [2 package, 10 oz each]. \
Both clients (ramekin-ui/src/utils/ingredientFormatting.ts and ramekin-ios/Ramekin/IngredientFormatting.swift) multiply every alternative's amount by the recipe scale, so scaling by 2 shows \"4 packages (20 oz each)\" instead of keeping 10 oz each (or showing a 40 oz total). \
Fix: don't scale an alternative whose unit ends in \" each\" (or convert it to a total before storing). \
This is deterministic client logic, so follow doc/client-logic-sharing.md: push it to the server if it fits, otherwise mirror tests with shared vectors on web and iOS. \
Also check that nutrition/catalog_calories doesn't treat \"10 oz each\" as the line's total weight. \
No make pipeline data/ diffs expected if the fix is client-side.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
